Lots of comments...  please pardon any misconceptions due to my (deliberately)
not having seriously read the code for ages.

o  Hitting Floating Eyes by accident
   What is needed is a user-option list of monsters to confirm hits on.
   The default would be "shopkeeper", but Greg Lewis and I would quickly
   change that to "shopkeeper,floating eye".

o  Terminal Rust
   How about a probabilistic solution?  Have a chance that items of -3 and
   worse fall apart in rusting attacks, just like +N items can melt on
   enchantment.  If bathing in a rust trap is considered to be an unfair
   exploitation of this rust-to-dust feature, have rust traps dry up--- 
   after all they are usually only a problem once.  I thoroughly agree with
   the poster who said this gives a much needed reason not to genocide rust 
   monsters.
   
o  Stormbringer
   Stormbringer only provided Elric with power (regeneration, and/or mana
   in hack terms?) when it killed something (quasi-vampiric regeneration
   in AD&D terms).  One way to implement this would be to regenerate its
   owner by 1hp when Stormbringer makes a drain--- this is rather 
   conservative, but Stormy is already quite powerful enough IMHO.
  
o  Aligned items in general
   Aligned items should certainly react adversely to users of the wrong
   alignment.  Leaping into a correctly aligned foes' hands is a nice
   suggestion.  Refusing to be used is good too.  This of course applies to 
   the monsters who pick up weapons as well.

o  Weapon restrictions, and classes
   Ahem.  Could all the people who want to turn Nethack into AD&D please
   desist?  Vicious evil gods demanding their priests only use blunt weapons
   indeed!  We hack-traditionalists would prefer that the only difference
   between the classes be their starting equipment, intrinsics and statistics,
   and that *all* of these properties be acquirable in the course of the game.
   In other words, "its the same game for all, but there are several ways
   of getting into it".

o  Installation
   If I compile "out of the box" on a vanilla 4.3BSD Vax/780, loading fails
   unable to find the v*printf family, who are not in libc.  Easy to fix,
   but a nit nevertheless.

Cheers, and salutations to the developers,
